#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# commonest

#% text
# `commonest(xs)` gives the elements of `xs` that occur most often, in order of first occurrence. `commonest(xs, n)` gives the `n` most frequent elements (ties broken by first occurrence), also in order of first occurrence.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
commonest([b, a, c, 2, a, b, 1, 2])
#% output
#= [b, a, 2]

#% cell
commonest([b, a, c, 2, a, b, 1, 2], 4)
#% output
#= [b, a, c, 2]

#% cell
commonest([1, 2, 2, 3, 3, 3, 4])
#% output
#= [3]

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `tally`, `counts`, `max_by`
